              "China on Friday announced plans to retaliate against the Trump administration with new tariffs on roughly $75 billion worth of US products and reinstated duties on American cars.\n\nThe Chinese finance ministry said in a statement that tariffs of 5% to 10% on more than 5,000 products would take effect in two batches, beginning September 1. The second tranche, which would include a 25% tax on US auto imports, was scheduled for December 15",
